Usage: rx AutoPack.rexx {drive:path}
(ie: Usage: rx AutoPack.rexx Cnet:)

A small Arexx script that will add to an archive all files that have
been modified since last run of AutoPack.

Doesn't look like LHARC's "-o (since date)" option has been activated
as of LHARC v1.40.  Thus this script works around it (as well as
saving the 'last-packed' date to the HD automatically.)

AutoPack does 4 things:
1)  Reads a preivously stored 'last-date packed'.
2)  Packs all files that have been changed since that date.
3)  Resaves current date for next usage in #1 above.
4)  Automatically creates 'Update.ReadMe' telling users 
    'this date' and 'last date' for this update, as well as 
    listing all the files.

Does several things we can't do with DMS:
1)  View inside the archive online.
2)  Save 300 D/Lers about 600,000 bytes each.  (Why tie up the system
    D/Ling 18,000,000 bytes THAT YOU ALREADY HAVE SITTING ON YOUR HD?)
    (Why pay the phone company if you are calling here from BFE?)
3)  Want to know exactly which files have/haven't been updated in
    this release?  Easy.  Every file in the LHA.
4)  Unpack directly to any sized partition on your HD.          
5)  Selectively unpack only any 1 (or more) files that you need.

*/

parse arg pathname                    /* Get CLI arg of full path */

LF='0a'x                              /* Line-feed char */
readme  = "t:UpDate.Readme"           /* LHA these files + include this list */
output  = "CnetNew"                   /* Resulting .LHA file */
pointer = "Env:" || output || ".date" /* Store date of last LHA here */

date2=translate(delstr(date('NORMAL'), 8, 2), "-", " ")  /* Today's date */

if(~exists(pointer)) then
   call WriteDate          /* If it's the 1st time AutoPack is run */

call ReadDate              /* Get last-pack date */

ADDRESS COMMAND "c:List >" || readme pathname "LFORMAT ""%f%s"" SINCE " date2
ADDRESS COMMAND "LZ -e -r -i" || readme "u" output   /* Compress */

call open(fp, readme, APPEND)       /* Add info to readme file */
writeCH(fp, LF "Today is" date2 || "." LF)
writeCH(fp, LF "All of the above files have been updated since the")
writeCH(fp, LF "last LHA release on" date1 || "." LF)
call close(fp)

ADDRESS COMMAND "LZ u" output readme  /* Add modified read-me & filelist */

call WriteDate    /* Update last-time-packed pointer */
exit

WriteDate:        /* Update last-time-packed pointer */
   call open(fp, pointer, WRITE)
   writeLN(fp, date2)     /* Date of this LHA as 01-Jan-92 */
   call close(fp)
   say LF "Storing" date2 "in" pointer LF
return

ReadDate:
   call open(fp, pointer, READ)
   date1=readLN(fp)               /* Date of last release as 01-Jan-92 */
   call close(fp)
   say LF "Getting last-pack date of" date1 "from" pointer LF
return

